User Identity maps each address on the network to the user logged on
from it, from the logon events of the Active Directory domain
controllers: NXLog CE on each sends them to OPNsense's own syslog-ng,
which takes them from the domain controllers' addresses alone. The
directory chosen in System: Access: Servers says which groups each user
is in. The addresses of each group chosen, and of each user named, are
kept in a pf table: an External alias in Firewall: Aliases for rules to
use. A mapping ends at the end of its lifetime, or when another device
takes the address. Where os-xgs-npu is installed, an address that joins
a table has its open connections cut. Off by default.

